# APEX FLOW CODEOWNERS
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern> <@owner> [<@owner2> ...]
# Owners are automatically requested as reviewers for PRs touching those paths.
# The LAST matching rule wins. More specific rules below override broader ones.
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# ── Default: all files require review from maintainer ─────────────────────────
*                          @nandan503

# ── Backend: any change to the Flask API ─────────────────────────────────────
/backend/                  @nandan503

# ── Auth / RBAC / Security — always require explicit maintainer review ────────
/backend/auth.py           @nandan503
/backend/config.py         @nandan503
/backend/logger.py         @nandan503

# ── Database schema — explicit review for any schema change ───────────────────
/backend/database.py       @nandan503

# ── CI / workflow — changes to automation pipeline require maintainer sign-off ─
/.github/                  @nandan503
/.pre-commit-config.yaml   @nandan503
/.semgrep.yml              @nandan503

# ── Dependency management — CVE exposure on every change ──────────────────────
/requirements.txt          @nandan503

# ── Security documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/docs/SECURITY_AUDIT.md    @nandan503
